# --- AI-HARP ---
# Simulation outputs: regenerate with reproduce.sh, never commit.
results/**/*.csv
results/**/*.npz
results/**/*.png
results/**/*.pdf
results/runs.csv
# ...except the paper's evidence base (campaign brief: "Commit runs.csv"), and
# the policy-independent risk-estimation table beside it. Both are fully
# regenerable (experiments/full_sweep.py, experiments/risk_estimation.py).
!results/runs.csv
!results/risk_estimation.csv
# ...the sparse band re-run on the SUMO backend, which is the evidence for the
# backend comparison (analysis/backend_compare.py) the paper reports, and that
# comparison's own output. Regenerable, but expensive: 14,400 SUMO runs.
!results/runs_sparse_sumo.csv
!results/backend_sparse_comparison.csv
# ...and the paper's figures. The campaign brief names results/figures/ as a
# deliverable, so a reader must be able to see them without first running the
# pipeline. Regenerable with analysis/report.py; PDF is the vector original.
!results/figures/*.pdf
!results/figures/*.png
cache/
mobility/_sumo_build/
runs/
checkpoints/
tb_logs/

